## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design privacy-preserving, offline-first collaborative systems at scale. It tests technical understanding of cryptographic protocols, peer-to-peer networking, CRDT algorithms, and cost-benefit analysis while considering regulatory compliance and user experience constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Privacy-preserving collaborative editing
- CRDT convergence and conflict-free resolution
- Peer-to-peer mesh topology and infrastructure costs
- End-to-end encryption with lifecycle key management
- Compliance logging and audit trail requirements
- Performance trade-offs between latency and device resource consumption

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple OR-Set CRDT merge (illustrative)
function mergeORSet(A, B) {
  const merged = new Set([...A.added, ...B.added]);
  [...A.removed, ...B.removed].forEach(item => merged.delete(item));
  return merged;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate a feature into a practical 12‑month CBA with edge constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Edge inference costs (latency, energy, memory)
- Privacy and data minimization
- Cloud review costs vs offline results
- Rollout strategy and drift/maintenance costs
- Break-even horizon selection

## Code Example
```javascript
function estimateCBA(modelSizeMB, perInferenceJ, inferencesPerMonth, cloudCostPerEvent) {
  const energyKJ = perInferenceJ * inferencesPerMonth;
  const yearlyEnergyCost = (energyKJ / 1000) * 0.9;
  const cloudYear = cloudCostPerEvent * inferencesPerMonth * 12;
  const total = modelSizeMB + yearlyEnergyCost + cloudYear;
  return total;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify drift/maintenance costs and retraining cadence?
- How would latency targets influence model size vs accuracy trade-offs?
- What metrics would you track to decide go/no-go?

